      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That distinction between potential growth and present emptiness is incredibly painful, and the feeling of having lost your inner light often signals a deep disconnection from your past self. Since nothing feels new or significant, it might help to temporarily release the pressure to be \"alive\" with current creativity and instead focus on preserving your integrity as the writer who already spent their light. Sometimes the most honest thing to do when you feel like a fraud is to admit that position just so you can rest the world of your own performance before you can ever speak again, authentically.",
